Fate's note is a writing note: do not carry into the narrative that Fate fixed, rewrote or struck the record against a ban. Do not open the history with "In Age N" and do not count the age numbers again and again: the record's age is already known; tell time through an event, a season, a generation. Do not describe the world's sound rules (vowels, diphthongs, suffixes). Do not write record numbers (like #12), stat names and values (like power 75), star glyphs or percentages in the text; say everything in the language of the narrative. If it has died or vanished, tell it in the past tense.

